Release Notes - RLM v17.0BL1  April 2025
______________________________________________

v17.0BL1 is available on Windows, Mac, and Linux systems.

All manuals are available on the Reprise Website at: https://reprisesoftware.com/docs/

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Notes on this release:
----------------------
    - Identity-Based Licensing has been added to RLM. Product entitlements can be obtained from RLM Cloud with just a username and password.
    - rlmutil now has methods to view and remove named users from named-user licenses.

Problems fixed in this release:
_______________________________

    - CVE-2021-37498
    - CVE-2021-37499
    - CVE-2021-44153
    - Fixed regression which caused RLM to not be able to retrieve hostid from hardware dongles
    - RLM will now locate license files when the filepath contains an @ symbol
    - Removed clock jump warning at startup of license server
    - Named user count is now displayed in the web interface

Known issues in this release
____________________________

    - License signing with rlmsign fails when the filename contains a non-ASCII character.
    - RLM Cloud web services API fails to retrieve log files if it contains wide/8-bit characters (can still retrieve log files via web portal).
    - Product returned from rlm_actinfo2() is incorrect if variable is not sized specifically.
    - RLM web interface performance may be slow when running RLM on Windows. Sentinel HASP drivers can be installed to improve this.
    - Unable to reset passwords without at least one login.

What's new
__________

    - 32-bit Linux is no longer supported
    - RLM will validate ISV binaries against a sha256 hash file generated during build
    
